@startuml 11a_state_playback
!include _style.puml
title Playback state machine - PlaybackController

state Stopped
state Playing {
  Playing : data / last_advance: Instant
  Playing : entry / request_repaint_after(frame_duration)
}

[*] --> Stopped
Stopped --> Playing : toggle_playback(now) [timeline.len() > 1 and no modal open]\n/ cancel/commit busy tool (ToolEvent::Cancel); last_advance = now
Stopped --> Stopped : toggle_playback(now) [timeline.len() == 1]\n/ ignored (Play button is disabled)
Playing --> Playing : tick(now) [elapsed = now - last_advance >= frame_duration]\n/ n = floor(elapsed / frame_duration);\n   last_advance += n * frame_duration;\n   target = selected + n; if looping target %= len; select(target)
Playing --> Stopped : tick(now) [!looping and selected + n >= len - 1]\n/ select(len - 1)
Playing --> Playing : tick(now) [elapsed < frame_duration]\n/ return Some(frame_duration - elapsed) for request_repaint_after
Playing --> Stopped : Pause button | toggle_playback
Playing --> Stopped : add / duplicate / delete / move frame, any layer command, paste, import, set background, undo, redo, fps change
Playing --> Stopped : click on a frame in the list
Playing --> Stopped : any modal opened | project closed

note bottom
  frame_duration = 1 / timeline.fps seconds (fps 1..=60).
  During Playing the canvas shows the selected frame read-only: no ToolEvent is dispatched, selection ants and tool overlays are hidden.
  Playing never writes to History and never marks the project dirty. Frame advance uses the frame's OWN background colour,
  so a per-frame background change is visible during playback.
  Every frame is drawn as the composite of ITS visible layers (hidden layers stay hidden).
  Starting playback begins at the currently selected frame (not at frame 1).
end note
@enduml

@startuml 11b_state_dirty
!include _style.puml
title Project dirty tracking (History.clean_marker)

state Clean
state Dirty

[*] --> Clean : project created or loaded\n/ clean_marker = Some(0)
Clean --> Dirty : execute(cmd) | record_applied(cmd) | redo()\n[clean_marker != Some(undo_stack.len()) afterwards]
Dirty --> Clean : mark_clean() after successful .aspr save\n[clean_marker = Some(undo_stack.len())]
Dirty --> Clean : undo() | redo()\n[clean_marker == Some(undo_stack.len()) afterwards]
Clean --> Dirty : undo()\n[undo_stack.len() != clean_marker afterwards]
Dirty --> Dirty : record_applied(cmd) [clean_marker > undo_stack.len() before it]\n/ clean_marker = None (the clean state is unreachable)

note bottom
  Dirty is a computed property: is_dirty() = clean_marker != Some(undo_stack.len()).
  Not dirty-making (never recorded): selection changes (outline-only move, invert, select all), copy, zoom/pan, tool / brush / colour / option changes,
  picking colours, brush library changes, switching the selected frame or layer, export, playback.
  Dirty-making: every Command (cell patches from paint / erase / fill / move / cut / clear, frame add/duplicate/delete/move, frame background, fps/loop,
  layer add/duplicate/delete/move, layer rename / visibility / opacity, paste, import, canvas resize).
  The window title shows "name *" when dirty. Save As to a NEW path also calls mark_clean() once written.
end note
@enduml

@startuml 11c_state_export_job
!include _style.puml
title Export job state machine (worker thread: ASCII image sequence or MP4, see ExportWorker in 07)

state Preparing
Preparing : entry / MP4: spawn ffmpeg, start the stderr drain thread | sequence: compute the file names (nothing is created yet)
state Encoding
Encoding : data / i: u32 (frames done), total: u32
Encoding : do / flatten frame i, then MP4: render + write RGBA bytes to ffmpeg stdin | sequence: encode .ascii and write {name}.part;   send Progress(i + 1, total)
state Finalizing
Finalizing : entry / MP4: close stdin, child.wait() | sequence: rename every {name}.part to {name}
state Cancelling
Cancelling : entry / MP4: kill child, delete {out}.part | sequence: delete every {name}.part written so far
state Failed
Failed : entry / MP4: kill child if alive, delete {out}.part | sequence: delete every {name}.part written so far;  send Failed(error)
state Finished
Finished : entry / MP4: rename {out}.part -> {out} | send Finished(path)   (path = the .mp4 file, or the folder of the sequence)
state Cancelled
Cancelled : entry / send Cancelled

[*] --> Preparing : start_mp4() | start_ascii_sequence()
Preparing --> Encoding : MP4: ffmpeg spawned | sequence: names ready
Preparing --> Failed : MP4: spawn error (FfmpegNotFound / Io)
Encoding --> Encoding : [i < total and !cancel] frame written
Encoding --> Cancelling : [cancel flag set] (checked before every frame)
Encoding --> Failed : MP4: stdin write error (ffmpeg died) | sequence: file write or encode error
Encoding --> Finalizing : [i == total]
Finalizing --> Finished : MP4: exit status == 0 | sequence: all renames ok
Finalizing --> Failed : MP4: exit status != 0 (FfmpegFailed with stderr tail) | sequence: a rename fails
Cancelling --> Cancelled
Finished --> [*]
Failed --> [*]
Cancelled --> [*]

note as ExportNote
  The UI thread never blocks on the job: AsciiPaintApp.poll_export_job() drains ExportMessage values once per egui frame.
  The Cancel button only sets the shared AtomicBool; the worker reacts before processing the next frame.
  Sequence export: final file names appear only in Finalizing, so a cancelled export or an encode / write error never leaves a half-written sequence and never
  destroys files that already existed under those names (only a failing rename inside Finalizing can leave a mix; the error names the file).
  Hidden layers are never part of any export.
end note
@enduml

@startuml 11d_state_import
!include _style.puml
title Import flow state machine (File > Import file...)

state ChoosingFile
ChoosingFile : entry / FileDialogs.pick_file(["txt", "ascii"])
state Decoding
Decoding : entry / Services.importer.load(path) -> ImportedFile (size in cells, warnings)
state ReviewFits
ReviewFits : entry / modal = Import(file, ink = current ink colour, fit = Fits)   buttons: [Import] [Cancel]
state ReviewTooBig
ReviewTooBig : entry / modal = Import(file, ink, fit = TooBig(suggested, cut_if_kept, cut_if_resized))\n   shows the SUGGESTION and what would be cut off   buttons: [Resize project and import] [Import without resizing] [Cancel]
state Applying
Applying : entry / session.import_content(file.to_buffer(ink), file.name, resize)
state ShowingError
ShowingError : entry / modal = Error(ImportError text)

[*] --> ChoosingFile : File > Import file...
ChoosingFile --> [*] : dialog cancelled
ChoosingFile --> Decoding : file chosen
Decoding --> ShowingError : Err(ImportError)
Decoding --> ReviewFits : Ok [project canvas.fit_content(file.width, file.height) == Fits]
Decoding --> ReviewTooBig : Ok [file wider OR taller than the project]
ReviewFits --> ReviewFits : ink swatch changed [plain text only]\n/ ink = colour
ReviewTooBig --> ReviewTooBig : ink swatch changed [plain text only]\n/ ink = colour
ReviewFits --> Applying : [Import]\n/ resize = None
ReviewTooBig --> Applying : [Resize project and import]\n/ resize = Some(suggested)  (grow only, max 1024 x 1024)
ReviewTooBig --> Applying : [Import without resizing]  (the user refuses the suggestion)\n/ resize = None; the layer is cut off at the page border
ReviewFits --> [*] : Cancel or Esc
ReviewTooBig --> [*] : Cancel or Esc
ShowingError --> [*] : OK
Applying --> [*] : done

note bottom
  Applying = ONE undo step (CompositeCommand "Import file" when the canvas grows, AddLayerCommand otherwise): a new layer above the active layer
  (named after the file) becomes active, its cells become the selection, the Move tool is activated in "Contents" mode so the layer can be dragged into place.
  Nothing is written to disk by an import. The playback is stopped when the dialog opens.
  A file that fits is added unchanged at the top-left corner (0, 0).
end note
@enduml
